IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `rawq-dates`
IMPORT `rawq-commencement`

-- Respect at Work and Other Matters Amendment Act 2024 (Queensland) -- as the PERSON WHO COMPLAINS meets it.
--
-- SEAT: the person who was subjected to an alleged contravention of the Anti-Discrimination Act 1991 (discrimination,
-- sexual harassment, harassment on the basis of sex, a hostile work environment, vilification and the like) and who
-- complains, or may complain, to the Queensland Human Rights Commissioner, alone or as a member of a class in a
-- representative complaint. "Has this change commenced?", "By when must I complain?", "Who may act as my agent?",
-- "Can I bring a representative complaint?", "Can I still complain on my own?", "Who has to prove what?", "Is what
-- happened to me covered?". No seat for the commissioner, the tribunal or the industrial relations commission.
--
-- This is an amending Act. Its operative effect for the complainant is the Anti-Discrimination Act 1991 as amended, and
-- the transitional provisions it inserts (chapter 11, part 10). The encoding takes the amended provisions from the
-- amending Act's own text (the "insert" and "omit, insert" words), and the commencement from s 2, read against the
-- Anti-Discrimination Act 1991 deposited beside it (rawq-commencement.l4).
--
-- The 1 July 2025 group of changes had not commenced on the deposited evidence (finding 1). Every question that turns on
-- it asks two plain facts: whether those changes have commenced, and the day they did. Judgments (whether a reasonable
-- person would have anticipated offence; whether there is a substantial common issue) are asked, never decided.
--
-- Every exported question takes plain facts (yes/no, dates, a choice from a list). The complaint period is a DEONTIC
-- rule run inside; no question takes a DEONTIC or an EVENT.
--
-- Unofficial version. Based on content from the Queensland Legislation website at 6 November 2026. (c) The State of
-- Queensland, CC BY 4.0. See SOURCE-LICENSE.md.
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Respect at Work and Other Matters Amendment Act 2024: the complainant's questions`

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `s 2 -- has the change commenced`
-- ===================================================================================================================

@export When does this change made by the Respect at Work and Other Matters Amendment Act 2024 (Queensland) commence, under its s 2 as passed? Some changes commenced on 1 December 2024 (s 2(1)), most of the rest were set for 1 July 2025 (s 2(2)), and part 11 follows a Commonwealth Act (s 2(3)). This answers from s 2 alone; ask "What is the commencement status" for what the Anti-Discrimination Act 1991 in force shows.
GIVEN `provision` IS A `Provision of the amending Act` @desc The change you are asking about, as a section or part of the amending Act with what it does (for example "s 29 (the 2-year complaint period, s 138)")
GIVETH A `When s 2 commences it`
`When does this change commence under s 2` MEANS
    `s 2 -- when it commences` `provision`

@export Had this change made by the Respect at Work and Other Matters Amendment Act 2024 (Queensland) commenced on a given day, under its s 2 as passed? Yes from 1 December 2024 for the s 2(1) group, from 1 July 2025 for the s 2(2) group; no answer where s 2 gives no day the deposited sources supply. As passed only: the 1 July 2025 group has in fact been deferred by later legislation (ask "What is the commencement status").
GIVEN `provision` IS A `Provision of the amending Act` @desc The change you are asking about, as a section or part of the amending Act with what it does
      `day asked` IS A DATE @desc The day you are asking about, as an ISO date such as 2025-07-01
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Had this change commenced on that day under s 2 as passed` MEANS
    `s 2 -- commenced by` `provision` `day asked`

@export What is the commencement status of this change made by the Respect at Work and Other Matters Amendment Act 2024 (Queensland)? s 2 as passed, checked against the Anti-Discrimination Act 1991 in force on 6 November 2026: the 1 December 2024 changes (mainly representative complaints, costs and the burden of proof) are in it; the 1 July 2025 changes (the 2-year complaint period, harassment on the basis of sex, the positive duty, new attributes and more) are not, so their commencement has been deferred by later legislation not deposited here.
GIVEN `provision` IS A `Provision of the amending Act` @desc The change you are asking about, as a section or part of the amending Act with what it does
GIVETH A `Commencement status`
`What is the commencement status of this change` MEANS
    `the commencement status of` `provision`

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `s 7 -- is my attribute protected`
-- ===================================================================================================================

-- s 7 of the Anti-Discrimination Act 1991 as amended by s 7 of the amending Act (s 7(1) to (5)): the list (a) to (x)
-- after renumbering. Schedule 1 "attribute means an attribute set out in section 7": a "means" definition, so a thing
-- not in the list is JUST FALSE kind. "Sexuality" becomes "sexual orientation" (s 7(2)): the same ground, renamed
-- (fork F4). "Family responsibilities" becomes "family, carer or kinship responsibilities" (s 7(3)); only the carer
-- and kinship part beyond the family is new (fork F5).
-- Schedule 1 "race includes" (s 52(1), (2)): the new definition adds "caste" to (b) and "(e) immigration or migration
-- status" to the former (a) colour, (b) descent or ancestry, (c) ethnicity or ethnic origin, (d) nationality or national
-- origin (1991 Act schedule 1 in force on 6 November 2026). Race is split in two: the former heads are an attribute
-- before and after; caste and immigration or migration status are named only from the 1 July 2025 group. Before then
-- the former definition "includes" without closing the list, so the answer is "not covered" (NOTHING kind), not "no"
-- (fork F16). The widened "trade union activity", "relation" and "parent" are not split (fork F17).
DECLARE `Attribute` IS ONE OF
    `sex`
    `relationship status`
    `pregnancy`
    `potential pregnancy (being able to, wanting to or being likely to become pregnant, or fertility treatment)`
    `parental status`
    `breastfeeding`
    `age`
    `race, as colour, descent or ancestry, ethnicity or ethnic origin, or nationality or national origin`
    `race, as caste or immigration or migration status`
    `impairment`
    `religious belief or religious activity`
    `political belief or activity`
    `trade union activity`
    `sex work activity`
    `gender identity`
    `sexual orientation (formerly sexuality)`
    `sex characteristics`
    `family responsibilities`
    `carer or kinship responsibilities, beyond responsibilities to my family`
    `subjection to domestic or family violence`
    `homelessness`
    `physical appearance (weight, size, height, a facial or body birthmark or scar, or another feature I did not choose)`
    `an expunged conviction`
    `an irrelevant criminal record`
    `an irrelevant medical record (including workers compensation claims)`
    `association with, or relation to, a person with any of these attributes`
    `a combination of 2 or more of these attributes`
    `something not in this list`

GIVEN `the attribute` IS AN `Attribute`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 7 -- added by the amending Act` `the attribute` IF
    CONSIDER `the attribute`
    WHEN `potential pregnancy (being able to, wanting to or being likely to become pregnant, or fertility treatment)` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `carer or kinship responsibilities, beyond responsibilities to my family` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `subjection to domestic or family violence` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `homelessness` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `physical appearance (weight, size, height, a facial or body birthmark or scar, or another feature I did not choose)` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an expunged conviction` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an irrelevant criminal record` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an irrelevant medical record (including workers compensation claims)` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a combination of 2 or more of these attributes` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

DECLARE `Is my attribute protected` IS ONE OF
    `yes: it is an attribute in s 7, before and after the amending Act`
    `yes: the amending Act added it to s 7, and that change was in force when the conduct happened`
    `no: the amending Act adds it to s 7, but that change was not in force when the conduct happened`
    `yes: the amending Act named it in the definition of race, and that change was in force when the conduct happened`
    `not covered: the amending Act names it in the definition of race, but that change was not in force when the conduct happened, and the former definition ("race includes" colour, descent or ancestry, ethnicity or ethnic origin, nationality or national origin) neither names nor excludes it`
    `no: it is not an attribute set out in s 7 (schedule 1, attribute)`

GIVEN `the attribute` IS AN `Attribute`
      `the day of the conduct` IS A DATE
      `the July 2025 changes have commenced` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day they commenced` IS A DATE
GIVETH AN `Is my attribute protected`
`s 7 -- is the attribute protected` `the attribute` `the day of the conduct` `the July 2025 changes have commenced` `the day they commenced` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the attribute` EQUALS `something not in this list`
        THEN `no: it is not an attribute set out in s 7 (schedule 1, attribute)`
        IF `the attribute` EQUALS `race, as caste or immigration or migration status`
        THEN IF `the July 2025 changes are in force on` `the July 2025 changes have commenced` `the day they commenced` `the day of the conduct`
             THEN `yes: the amending Act named it in the definition of race, and that change was in force when the conduct happened`
             ELSE `not covered: the amending Act names it in the definition of race, but that change was not in force when the conduct happened, and the former definition ("race includes" colour, descent or ancestry, ethnicity or ethnic origin, nationality or national origin) neither names nor excludes it`
        IF NOT (`s 7 -- added by the amending Act` `the attribute`)
        THEN `yes: it is an attribute in s 7, before and after the amending Act`
        IF `the July 2025 changes are in force on` `the July 2025 changes have commenced` `the day they commenced` `the day of the conduct`
        THEN `yes: the amending Act added it to s 7, and that change was in force when the conduct happened`
        OTHERWISE `no: the amending Act adds it to s 7, but that change was not in force when the conduct happened`

@export Is discrimination on the basis of this attribute prohibited by the Anti-Discrimination Act 1991 (Queensland), s 7, as the Respect at Work and Other Matters Amendment Act 2024 amends it? The amending Act adds potential pregnancy, carer and kinship responsibilities, domestic or family violence, homelessness, physical appearance, expunged convictions, irrelevant criminal and medical records and combinations of attributes, and names caste and immigration or migration status in the definition of race, from the commencement of its 1 July 2025 group of changes.
GIVEN `attribute` IS AN `Attribute` @desc The attribute you were treated badly for (choose "something not in this list" if none fits)
      `day of conduct` IS A DATE @desc The day the conduct happened, as an ISO date
      `July 2025 changes commenced` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the changes the amending Act set for 1 July 2025 have commenced; they were not in the Anti-Discrimination Act 1991 in force on 6 November 2026, so check the Queensland legislation register
      `July 2025 changes day` IS A DATE @desc If they have commenced, the day they did, as an ISO date; otherwise any date
GIVETH AN `Is my attribute protected`
`Is my attribute protected` MEANS
    `s 7 -- is the attribute protected` `attribute` `day of conduct` `July 2025 changes commenced` `July 2025 changes day`

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `ss 117A, 120, 120A to 120E -- harassment on the basis of sex`
-- ===================================================================================================================

-- new s 120(1): harassment on the basis of sex "happens if" a person (a) engages in unwelcome conduct of a demeaning
-- nature in relation to another person; and (b) does so on the basis of the other person's sex, a characteristic of or
-- imputed to that sex, a sex presumed, or a sex the person has been; and (c) with intent to offend, humiliate or
-- intimidate, or where a reasonable person would have anticipated the possibility that the other person would be
-- offended, humiliated or intimidated. (2): sex need be only one of the reasons. A definition: JUST FALSE kind when a
-- limb fails. The reasonable person's anticipation is a judgment (s 117A, the former s 120, lists the relevant
-- circumstances): asked.
DECLARE `On what basis` IS ONE OF
    `my sex`
    `a characteristic that people of my sex generally have`
    `a characteristic often imputed to people of my sex`
    `a sex they presumed me to be, or to have been`
    `a sex I have been, though I am not that sex now`
    `none of these`

GIVEN `unwelcome` IS A BOOLEAN
      `demeaning` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the basis` IS AN `On what basis`
      `intended to offend humiliate or intimidate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a reasonable person would have anticipated it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 120 -- harassment on the basis of sex` `unwelcome` `demeaning` `the basis` `intended to offend humiliate or intimidate` `a reasonable person would have anticipated it` IF
    `limb (a)` AND `limb (b)` AND `limb (c)`
    WHERE
        `limb (a)` MEANS `unwelcome` AND `demeaning`
        `limb (b)` MEANS NOT (`the basis` EQUALS `none of these`)
        `limb (c)` MEANS `intended to offend humiliate or intimidate` OR `a reasonable person would have anticipated it`

-- Division 2: whom each prohibition protects, from the seat of the person harassed. "Person conducting a business or
-- undertaking" is borrowed from the Work Health and Safety Act 2011 s 5 (schedule 1): asked.
DECLARE `How I stand to the harasser` IS ONE OF
    `they conduct a business or undertaking in which I work or seek work`
    `they conduct a business or undertaking, and harassed me in connection with conducting it`
    `we are workers in the same business or undertaking`
    `they work in a business or undertaking in which I seek work`
    `they work in a business or undertaking, and harassed me in connection with their work there`
    `I conduct a business or undertaking, or work in one`
    `we are both members of the same organisation of workers or employers, or of people in an industry, profession, trade or business`
    `I am seeking membership of an organisation of which they are a member`
    `they have power to grant, renew or extend a professional, trade or business qualification or authorisation I seek`
    `none of these`

GIVEN `how I stand` IS A `How I stand to the harasser`
GIVETH A STRING
`ss 120A to 120E -- the prohibition` `how I stand` MEANS
    CONSIDER `how I stand`
    WHEN `they conduct a business or undertaking in which I work or seek work` THEN "s 120A(a), (b)"
    WHEN `they conduct a business or undertaking, and harassed me in connection with conducting it` THEN "s 120A(c)"
    WHEN `we are workers in the same business or undertaking` THEN "s 120B(a)"
    WHEN `they work in a business or undertaking in which I seek work` THEN "s 120B(b)"
    WHEN `they work in a business or undertaking, and harassed me in connection with their work there` THEN "s 120B(c)"
    WHEN `I conduct a business or undertaking, or work in one` THEN "s 120C"
    WHEN `we are both members of the same organisation of workers or employers, or of people in an industry, profession, trade or business` THEN "s 120D(a)"
    WHEN `I am seeking membership of an organisation of which they are a member` THEN "s 120D(b)"
    WHEN `they have power to grant, renew or extend a professional, trade or business qualification or authorisation I seek` THEN "s 120E"
    OTHERWISE ""

DECLARE `Was it harassment on the basis of sex that the Act prohibits` IS ONE OF
    `yes: harassment on the basis of sex (s 120), prohibited by the section named`
        HAS `section` IS A STRING
    `no: the conduct does not meet s 120 (it must be unwelcome and demeaning, on the basis of sex, and intended to offend, humiliate or intimidate or such that a reasonable person would have anticipated that)`
    `not covered: it meets s 120, but chapter 3 part 3 has no prohibition for how you stand to the person (other provisions may still apply, s 120AA)`
    `no: chapter 3 part 3 was not in force when the conduct happened`

GIVEN `unwelcome` IS A BOOLEAN
      `demeaning` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the basis` IS AN `On what basis`
      `intended` IS A BOOLEAN
      `anticipated` IS A BOOLEAN
      `how I stand` IS A `How I stand to the harasser`
      `the day of the conduct` IS A DATE
      `the July 2025 changes have commenced` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day they commenced` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Was it harassment on the basis of sex that the Act prohibits`
`ch 3 pt 3 -- harassment on the basis of sex` `unwelcome` `demeaning` `the basis` `intended` `anticipated` `how I stand` `the day of the conduct` `the July 2025 changes have commenced` `the day they commenced` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the July 2025 changes are in force on` `the July 2025 changes have commenced` `the day they commenced` `the day of the conduct`)
        THEN `no: chapter 3 part 3 was not in force when the conduct happened`
        IF NOT (`s 120 -- harassment on the basis of sex` `unwelcome` `demeaning` `the basis` `intended` `anticipated`)
        THEN `no: the conduct does not meet s 120 (it must be unwelcome and demeaning, on the basis of sex, and intended to offend, humiliate or intimidate or such that a reasonable person would have anticipated that)`
        IF `how I stand` EQUALS `none of these`
        THEN `not covered: it meets s 120, but chapter 3 part 3 has no prohibition for how you stand to the person (other provisions may still apply, s 120AA)`
        OTHERWISE `yes: harassment on the basis of sex (s 120), prohibited by the section named` (`ss 120A to 120E -- the prohibition` `how I stand`)

@export Was what happened to me harassment on the basis of sex that the Anti-Discrimination Act 1991 (Queensland) prohibits, under chapter 3 part 3 as inserted by the Respect at Work and Other Matters Amendment Act 2024 s 18? It needs unwelcome, demeaning conduct on the basis of sex, done to offend, humiliate or intimidate or where a reasonable person would have anticipated that, by someone the part names (an employer or business, a co-worker, a member of the same organisation, a qualifying body). The part commences with the 1 July 2025 group of changes.
GIVEN `unwelcome` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the conduct was unwelcome to you
      `demeaning` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the conduct was of a demeaning nature
      `basis` IS AN `On what basis` @desc What the conduct was based on: your sex; a characteristic people of your sex generally have; one often imputed to them; a sex they presumed you to be; a sex you have been; or none of these (it need be only one of their reasons)
      `intended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether they meant to offend, humiliate or intimidate you
      `anticipated` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a reasonable person would have anticipated the possibility that you would be offended, humiliated or intimidated (a judgment for the commission or tribunal; answer as you expect it to be found)
      `how I stand` IS A `How I stand to the harasser` @desc How you stand to the person who did it (for example they run the business you work in, or you are co-workers)
      `day of conduct` IS A DATE @desc The day the conduct happened, as an ISO date
      `July 2025 changes commenced` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the changes the amending Act set for 1 July 2025 have commenced; they were not in the Anti-Discrimination Act 1991 in force on 6 November 2026, so check the Queensland legislation register
      `July 2025 changes day` IS A DATE @desc If they have commenced, the day they did, as an ISO date; otherwise any date
GIVETH A `Was it harassment on the basis of sex that the Act prohibits`
`Was it harassment on the basis of sex` MEANS
    `ch 3 pt 3 -- harassment on the basis of sex` `unwelcome` `demeaning` `basis` `intended` `anticipated` `how I stand` `day of conduct` `July 2025 changes commenced` `July 2025 changes day`

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `s 124E -- a work environment hostile on the basis of sex`
-- ===================================================================================================================

-- new s 124E(1) "A person must not subject another person to a work environment that is hostile on the basis of sex."
-- (2) "subjects ... if" (a) the first person engages in conduct in a place where either or both work; and (b) the
-- second person is at the place at the time or after; and (c) a reasonable person would have anticipated the
-- possibility that the conduct would create a work environment offensive, humiliating or intimidating to a person of
-- the second person's sex on the basis of sex or a characteristic of or imputed to that sex. (3) sex need be only one
-- reason. (c) is a judgment (s 124F lists the circumstances): asked. A definition: JUST FALSE kind when a limb fails.
DECLARE `Was I subjected to a hostile work environment` IS ONE OF
    `yes: you were subjected to a work environment hostile on the basis of sex, which s 124E(1) prohibits`
    `no: the conduct does not meet s 124E(2)`
    `no: s 124E was not in force when the conduct happened`

GIVEN `conduct where either works` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I was there at the time or after` IS A BOOLEAN
      `anticipated` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of the conduct` IS A DATE
      `the July 2025 changes have commenced` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day they commenced` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Was I subjected to a hostile work environment`
`s 124E -- hostile work environment` `conduct where either works` `I was there at the time or after` `anticipated` `the day of the conduct` `the July 2025 changes have commenced` `the day they commenced` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the July 2025 changes are in force on` `the July 2025 changes have commenced` `the day they commenced` `the day of the conduct`)
        THEN `no: s 124E was not in force when the conduct happened`
        IF `conduct where either works` AND `I was there at the time or after` AND `anticipated`
        THEN `yes: you were subjected to a work environment hostile on the basis of sex, which s 124E(1) prohibits`
        OTHERWISE `no: the conduct does not meet s 124E(2)`

@export Was I subjected to a work environment hostile on the basis of sex, which the Anti-Discrimination Act 1991 (Queensland) s 124E prohibits (inserted by the Respect at Work and Other Matters Amendment Act 2024 s 22)? The conduct must happen in a place where you or the person (or both) work, you must be there then or after, and a reasonable person would have anticipated it could make the workplace offensive, humiliating or intimidating to a person of your sex because of sex. It commences with the 1 July 2025 group of changes.
GIVEN `conduct at a workplace` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person engaged in the conduct in a place where you, they, or both of you work
      `I was there` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were at that place when the conduct happened or afterwards
      `anticipated` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a reasonable person, having regard to all the circumstances (how serious it was, whether it was repeated, the person's role or authority), would have anticipated the possibility that it would make the work environment offensive, humiliating or intimidating to a person of your sex because of sex or a characteristic of that sex (a judgment for the commission or tribunal)
      `day of conduct` IS A DATE @desc The day the conduct happened, as an ISO date
      `July 2025 changes commenced` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the changes the amending Act set for 1 July 2025 have commenced; they were not in the Anti-Discrimination Act 1991 in force on 6 November 2026, so check the Queensland legislation register
      `July 2025 changes day` IS A DATE @desc If they have commenced, the day they did, as an ISO date; otherwise any date
GIVETH A `Was I subjected to a hostile work environment`
`Was I subjected to a hostile work environment` MEANS
    `s 124E -- hostile work environment` `conduct at a workplace` `I was there` `anticipated` `day of conduct` `July 2025 changes commenced` `July 2025 changes day`

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `ch 5C -- the positive duty`
-- ===================================================================================================================

-- new s 131I(1) "This section applies to a person who, under chapter 2, 3, 4 or 5, must not engage in discrimination,
-- sexual harassment, harassment on the basis of sex or other objectionable conduct." (2) "However, this section
-- applies to an individual only if the individual is a person conducting a business or undertaking." (3) the duty.
-- (1) is a scope limit with no "only": outside it, "not covered" (NOTHING kind); (2) "only if": JUST FALSE kind.
-- s 131H note and schedule 1 "contravention" (which s 52(4) amends to add harassment on the basis of sex, not the
-- positive duty): a breach of the duty is not a contravention a person may complain about under chapter 7 part 1; the
-- commissioner may investigate and enforce it under chapter 7 part 1A (s 131H(2)(b)).
DECLARE `Does the positive duty protect me` IS ONE OF
    `yes: they must take reasonable and proportionate measures to eliminate discrimination and harassment as far as possible (s 131I(3)); you cannot complain of a breach yourself, but the commissioner may investigate and enforce it (chapter 7 part 1A)`
    `no: an individual owes the duty only if they conduct a business or undertaking (s 131I(2))`
    `not covered: they are not under a chapter 2, 3, 4 or 5 prohibition towards people like you (s 131I(1))`
    `no: chapter 5C was not in force on that day`

GIVEN `bound by a prohibition` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an individual` IS A BOOLEAN
      `conducts a business or undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day asked` IS A DATE
      `the July 2025 changes have commenced` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day they commenced` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Does the positive duty protect me`
`s 131I -- the positive duty` `bound by a prohibition` `an individual` `conducts a business or undertaking` `the day asked` `the July 2025 changes have commenced` `the day they commenced` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the July 2025 changes are in force on` `the July 2025 changes have commenced` `the day they commenced` `the day asked`)
        THEN `no: chapter 5C was not in force on that day`
        IF NOT (`bound by a prohibition`)
        THEN `not covered: they are not under a chapter 2, 3, 4 or 5 prohibition towards people like you (s 131I(1))`
        IF `an individual` AND (NOT (`conducts a business or undertaking`))
        THEN `no: an individual owes the duty only if they conduct a business or undertaking (s 131I(2))`
        OTHERWISE `yes: they must take reasonable and proportionate measures to eliminate discrimination and harassment as far as possible (s 131I(3)); you cannot complain of a breach yourself, but the commissioner may investigate and enforce it (chapter 7 part 1A)`

@export Does the person or organisation I deal with (my employer, school, landlord, service provider) owe the positive duty under the Anti-Discrimination Act 1991 (Queensland) chapter 5C, inserted by the Respect at Work and Other Matters Amendment Act 2024 s 25, and can I complain if they breach it? Anyone under a prohibition in chapters 2 to 5 owes it (an individual only if they conduct a business or undertaking). A breach is not something you can complain about yourself; the commissioner may investigate and enforce it. It commences with the 1 July 2025 group.
GIVEN `bound by a prohibition` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Act's prohibitions of discrimination, sexual harassment, harassment on the basis of sex or other objectionable conduct bind them in their dealings with people like you (for example as an employer, educator, landlord or provider of goods or services)
      `an individual` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether they are an individual (a natural person) rather than a company, partnership, association or public body
      `conducts a business or undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether they are a person conducting a business or undertaking, in the sense of the Work Health and Safety Act 2011 s 5
      `day asked` IS A DATE @desc The day you are asking about, as an ISO date
      `July 2025 changes commenced` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the changes the amending Act set for 1 July 2025 have commenced; they were not in the Anti-Discrimination Act 1991 in force on 6 November 2026, so check the Queensland legislation register
      `July 2025 changes day` IS A DATE @desc If they have commenced, the day they did, as an ISO date; otherwise any date
GIVETH A `Does the positive duty protect me`
`Does the positive duty protect me` MEANS
    `s 131I -- the positive duty` `bound by a prohibition` `an individual` `conducts a business or undertaking` `day asked` `July 2025 changes commenced` `July 2025 changes day`

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `ss 138, 283 -- by when must I complain`
-- ===================================================================================================================

-- former s 138(1) "a person is only entitled to make a complaint within 1 year of the alleged contravention".
-- new s 138(1) (s 29(1)) "... within 2 years after the alleged contravention of the Act (the complaint period)".
-- s 138(2) (both): after that, the commissioner must accept the complaint only if satisfied the complainant has shown
-- good cause; otherwise not accept it (subject to s 141A).
-- new s 283(1) "New section 138 does not apply in relation to an alleged contravention of the Act that happened more
-- than 1 year before the commencement." (2) former ss 138, 141A and 175 apply to it. "The commencement" is that of
-- s 283 (s 282), in the 1 July 2025 group; asked. A complaint made before the new s 138 is in force meets the former.
-- "More than 1 year before": the day 1 year after the contravention is before the commencement day (fork F9).
DECLARE `Which s 138 applies` IS ONE OF
    `former s 138: 1 year after the alleged contravention`
    `new s 138: 2 years after the alleged contravention (the complaint period)`

GIVEN `the day of the contravention` IS A DATE
      `the day they commenced` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 283(1) -- more than 1 year before the commencement` `the day of the contravention` `the day they commenced` IF
    `the day` (`the date` 1 `years after` `the day of the contravention`) `is before` `the day they commenced`

GIVEN `the day of the contravention` IS A DATE
      `the day of the complaint` IS A DATE
      `the July 2025 changes have commenced` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day they commenced` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Which s 138 applies`
`ss 138, 283 -- which time limit applies` `the day of the contravention` `the day of the complaint` `the July 2025 changes have commenced` `the day they commenced` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the July 2025 changes are in force on` `the July 2025 changes have commenced` `the day they commenced` `the day of the complaint`)
        THEN `former s 138: 1 year after the alleged contravention`
        IF `s 283(1) -- more than 1 year before the commencement` `the day of the contravention` `the day they commenced`
        THEN `former s 138: 1 year after the alleged contravention`
        OTHERWISE `new s 138: 2 years after the alleged contravention (the complaint period)`

GIVEN `which` IS A `Which s 138 applies`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the years allowed under` `which` MEANS
    CONSIDER `which`
    WHEN `former s 138: 1 year after the alleged contravention` THEN 1
    OTHERWISE 2

-- The entitlement as a rule: I DO make my complaint WITHIN the days the time limit allows, LEST the time is not met.
-- The BREACH marks only that the time was not met (s 138(2) then applies): not complaining is not a wrong.
DECLARE `Complainant` IS ONE OF `I`
DECLARE `Step` IS ONE OF `make my complaint to the commissioner`

GIVEN `the days allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Complainant` `Step`
`s 138(1) -- complain within the time limit` `the days allowed` MEANS
    PARTY `I`
    DO `make my complaint to the commissioner`
    WITHIN `the days allowed`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `I` BECAUSE "the complaint was not made within the time s 138(1) allows; s 138(2) lets the commissioner accept it only if satisfied the complainant has shown good cause"

-- Runs the rule over what happened. On the stable l4 a CONSIDER on an EVALTRACE can match FULFILLED but not BREACH.
-- It takes a DEONTIC value, so it is never exported.
GIVEN `the rule` IS A DEONTIC `Complainant` `Step`
      `the time it was done` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `complained in time under` `the rule` `at` `the time it was done` IF
    CONSIDER EVALTRACE `the rule` 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL `the time it was done`), (EVENT `I` `make my complaint to the commissioner` `the time it was done`))
    WHEN FULFILLED THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the day of the contravention` IS A DATE
      `the July 2025 changes have commenced` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day they commenced` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 138(1) -- the last day to complain` `the day of the contravention` `the July 2025 changes have commenced` `the day they commenced` MEANS
    `the date` (`the years allowed under` `which`) `years after` `the day of the contravention`
    WHERE
        `which` MEANS
            IF `the July 2025 changes have commenced` AND (NOT (`s 283(1) -- more than 1 year before the commencement` `the day of the contravention` `the day they commenced`))
            THEN `new s 138: 2 years after the alleged contravention (the complaint period)`
            ELSE `former s 138: 1 year after the alleged contravention`

DECLARE `Am I in time to complain` IS ONE OF
    `yes, in time under former s 138(1): within 1 year after the alleged contravention`
    `yes, in time under new s 138(1): within the 2-year complaint period`
    `no, out of time: the commissioner must not accept the complaint unless satisfied you have shown good cause (s 138(2)); s 141A may let the commissioner defer that decision where other contraventions in the complaint are in time`

GIVEN `the day of the contravention` IS A DATE
      `the day of the complaint` IS A DATE
      `the July 2025 changes have commenced` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day they commenced` IS A DATE
GIVETH AN `Am I in time to complain`
`s 138 -- am I in time` `the day of the contravention` `the day of the complaint` `the July 2025 changes have commenced` `the day they commenced` MEANS
    IF `the day` `the day of the complaint` `is before` `the day of the contravention`
    THEN `in time` `which`
    ELSE IF `complained in time under` (`s 138(1) -- complain within the time limit` (`the days from` `the day of the contravention` `to` `the last day`)) `at` (`the days from` `the day of the contravention` `to` `the day of the complaint`)
         THEN `in time` `which`
         ELSE `no, out of time: the commissioner must not accept the complaint unless satisfied you have shown good cause (s 138(2)); s 141A may let the commissioner defer that decision where other contraventions in the complaint are in time`
    WHERE
        `which` MEANS `ss 138, 283 -- which time limit applies` `the day of the contravention` `the day of the complaint` `the July 2025 changes have commenced` `the day they commenced`
        `the last day` MEANS `the date` (`the years allowed under` `which`) `years after` `the day of the contravention`
        GIVEN w IS A `Which s 138 applies`
        `in time` w MEANS
            CONSIDER w
            WHEN `former s 138: 1 year after the alleged contravention` THEN `yes, in time under former s 138(1): within 1 year after the alleged contravention`
            OTHERWISE `yes, in time under new s 138(1): within the 2-year complaint period`

@export Am I in time to complain to the Queensland Human Rights Commissioner under the Anti-Discrimination Act 1991 s 138? It is 1 year after the alleged contravention until the Respect at Work and Other Matters Amendment Act 2024 s 29 commences, and 2 years after once it has (s 283 keeps 1 year for a contravention more than 1 year before that commencement). s 29 was set for 1 July 2025 but was not in force on 6 November 2026. Out of time, the commissioner may accept a complaint only for good cause.
GIVEN `day of contravention` IS A DATE @desc The day the alleged contravention happened, as an ISO date such as 2025-03-14
      `day of complaint` IS A DATE @desc The day you made, or will make, your complaint to the commissioner, as an ISO date
      `July 2025 changes commenced` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the changes the amending Act set for 1 July 2025 (including the 2-year time limit) have commenced; they were not in the Anti-Discrimination Act 1991 in force on 6 November 2026, so check the Queensland legislation register
      `July 2025 changes day` IS A DATE @desc If they have commenced, the day they did, as an ISO date; otherwise any date
GIVETH AN `Am I in time to complain`
`Am I in time to complain` MEANS
    `s 138 -- am I in time` `day of contravention` `day of complaint` `July 2025 changes commenced` `July 2025 changes day`

@export By when must I complain to the Queensland Human Rights Commissioner under the Anti-Discrimination Act 1991 s 138, as the Respect at Work and Other Matters Amendment Act 2024 changes it? The last day of the time limit: 1 year after the alleged contravention, or 2 years once the amending Act's s 29 has commenced, unless the contravention happened more than 1 year before that commencement (s 283). If s 29 has not yet commenced, the answer is 1 year, and would become 2 years if s 29 commences before that day passes. Where the answer is the 2-year day, a complaint made before s 29 commences is also in time, because it is then within the former 1 year (ask "Am I in time" for a given complaint day).
GIVEN `day of contravention` IS A DATE @desc The day the alleged contravention happened, as an ISO date
      `July 2025 changes commenced` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the changes the amending Act set for 1 July 2025 (including the 2-year time limit) have commenced; they were not in the Anti-Discrimination Act 1991 in force on 6 November 2026, so check the Queensland legislation register
      `July 2025 changes day` IS A DATE @desc If they have commenced, the day they did, as an ISO date; otherwise any date
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must I complain` MEANS
    `s 138(1) -- the last day to complain` `day of contravention` `July 2025 changes commenced` `July 2025 changes day`

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `ss 134(2), 284 -- who may act as my agent`
-- ===================================================================================================================

-- s 134(1)(b): an agent of the person subjected to the contravention may complain. new s 134(2) (s 28(2), (6)):
-- "However, for a complaint that wholly or partly relates to a work-related matter, a person's agent for subsection
-- (1)(b) can not be an employee or officer of, or acting for, an entity (other than a registered organisation) that
-- purports to represent the industrial interests of employees or employers." A flat negative: JUST FALSE kind.
-- new s 284: "New section 134(2) does not apply in relation to a complaint made before the commencement." s 28(2)
-- is in the 1 July 2025 group (only s 28(1) is in s 2(1)).
DECLARE `My agent` IS ONE OF
    `a person not connected with a body that represents industrial interests (for example a lawyer, relative or advocate)`
    `an employee or officer of, or a person acting for, a registered organisation (a union or employer body registered under the Industrial Relations Act 2016 or the Fair Work (Registered Organisations) Act 2009)`
    `an employee or officer of, or a person acting for, an unregistered body that claims to represent the industrial interests of employees or employers`

DECLARE `Can this person complain for me as my agent` IS ONE OF
    `yes: an agent may complain for you (s 134(1)(b))`
    `no: for a work-related complaint, your agent cannot be from a body other than a registered organisation that claims to represent industrial interests (s 134(2))`

GIVEN `the agent` IS A `My agent`
      `work-related` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of the complaint` IS A DATE
      `the July 2025 changes have commenced` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day they commenced` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Can this person complain for me as my agent`
`ss 134, 284 -- my agent` `the agent` `work-related` `the day of the complaint` `the July 2025 changes have commenced` `the day they commenced` MEANS
    IF      `work-related`
        AND (`the agent` EQUALS `an employee or officer of, or a person acting for, an unregistered body that claims to represent the industrial interests of employees or employers`)
        AND `the July 2025 changes are in force on` `the July 2025 changes have commenced` `the day they commenced` `the day of the complaint`
    THEN `no: for a work-related complaint, your agent cannot be from a body other than a registered organisation that claims to represent industrial interests (s 134(2))`
    ELSE `yes: an agent may complain for you (s 134(1)(b))`

@export Can this person make my anti-discrimination complaint for me as my agent (Anti-Discrimination Act 1991 (Queensland) s 134, as the Respect at Work and Other Matters Amendment Act 2024 s 28 changes it)? An agent may complain for you; but for a complaint that is wholly or partly work-related, the agent cannot be from a body (other than a registered union or employer organisation) that claims to represent industrial interests. That rule commences with the 1 July 2025 group and does not reach complaints made before it (s 284).
GIVEN `agent` IS A `My agent` @desc Who would act for you: a person not connected with an industrial body; someone from a registered organisation; or someone from an unregistered body that claims to represent industrial interests
      `work-related` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your complaint relates, wholly or partly, to work or the work-related area
      `day of complaint` IS A DATE @desc The day the complaint was or will be made, as an ISO date
      `July 2025 changes commenced` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the changes the amending Act set for 1 July 2025 have commenced; they were not in the Anti-Discrimination Act 1991 in force on 6 November 2026, so check the Queensland legislation register
      `July 2025 changes day` IS A DATE @desc If they have commenced, the day they did, as an ISO date; otherwise any date
GIVETH A `Can this person complain for me as my agent`
`Can this person complain for me as my agent` MEANS
    `ss 134, 284 -- my agent` `agent` `work-related` `day of complaint` `July 2025 changes commenced` `July 2025 changes day`

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `ss 146, 285 -- representative complaints`
-- ===================================================================================================================

-- new s 285: a complaint accepted before 1 December 2024 that, immediately before, was a representative complaint
-- still being dealt with by the commissioner or the tribunal continues under former chapter 7 parts 1 and 2 (not
-- deposited here). A condition the text fixes: the answers below say "not covered" for such a complaint.
GIVEN `accepted before 1 December 2024` IS A BOOLEAN
      `representative then` IS A BOOLEAN
      `still being dealt with then` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 285 -- the former law continues` `accepted before 1 December 2024` `representative then` `still being dealt with then` IF
    `accepted before 1 December 2024` AND `representative then` AND `still being dealt with then`

DECLARE `Which law governs the representative complaint` IS ONE OF
    `the former chapter 7, parts 1 and 2 continue to govern it, as if the amending Act had not been enacted (s 285(2)); the commissioner or tribunal may still give directions to bring it into line with the new law (s 285(3))`
    `the new law governs it (the amending Act, ss 31, 37, 38, 46 to 48, from 1 December 2024)`

@export Does the old law still govern a representative complaint I am part of, after the Respect at Work and Other Matters Amendment Act 2024 replaced the representative complaint provisions of the Anti-Discrimination Act 1991 (Queensland) on 1 December 2024 (s 285)? The old law continues for a representative complaint accepted before 1 December 2024 and still with the commissioner or the tribunal immediately before that day.
GIVEN `accepted before 1 December 2024` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the commissioner accepted the complaint before 1 December 2024
      `representative then` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, immediately before 1 December 2024, it was a representative complaint (made on behalf of a class of people)
      `still being dealt with then` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, immediately before 1 December 2024, the commissioner was still dealing with it, or it had been referred to the tribunal and the tribunal was still dealing with it
GIVETH A `Which law governs the representative complaint`
`Which law governs the representative complaint` MEANS
    IF `s 285 -- the former law continues` `accepted before 1 December 2024` `representative then` `still being dealt with then`
    THEN `the former chapter 7, parts 1 and 2 continue to govern it, as if the amending Act had not been enacted (s 285(2)); the commissioner or tribunal may still give directions to bring it into line with the new law (s 285(3))`
    ELSE `the new law governs it (the amending Act, ss 31, 37, 38, 46 to 48, from 1 December 2024)`

-- new s 146(1): a person may make a representative complaint for a class of which the person is a member "if" (a) all
-- members may complain under s 134(1)(a) about the alleged contravention; and (b) all their complaints (i) arise out of
-- conduct of the same person, (ii) arise out of the same, similar or related circumstances, and (iii) give rise to a
-- substantial common issue of law or fact. (3) no consent of class members needed. "if": JUST FALSE when a limb fails.
-- "a class of persons of which the person is a member" limits the grant in its own wording, before the "if": a person
-- outside the class is outside the grant, NOTHING (2026-11-04 ruling; fork F18).
-- Before 1 December 2024 the former s 146 applied (not deposited): NOTHING.
GIVEN `I am a member of the class` IS A BOOLEAN
      `all members could complain` IS A BOOLEAN
      `same respondent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `same or related circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN
      `substantial common issue` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of the complaint` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 146(1) -- I may make a representative complaint` `I am a member of the class` `all members could complain` `same respondent` `same or related circumstances` `substantial common issue` `the day of the complaint` MEANS
    IF `the day` `the day of the complaint` `is before` `1 December 2024`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF NOT (`I am a member of the class`)
         THEN NOTHING
         ELSE JUST (    `all members could complain`
                    AND (`same respondent` AND `same or related circumstances` AND `substantial common issue`))

@export Can I make a representative complaint to the Queensland Human Rights Commissioner on behalf of a class of people I belong to (Anti-Discrimination Act 1991 s 146(1), inserted by the Respect at Work and Other Matters Amendment Act 2024 s 31 from 1 December 2024)? Every member must be able to complain about the alleged contravention, and all their complaints must arise from the same person's conduct and the same, similar or related circumstances, and share a substantial common issue. Members need not consent. No answer if you are not a member of the class, or for a complaint made before 1 December 2024.
GIVEN `I am a member` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are yourself a member of the class you would complain for
      `all could complain` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether every member of the class was subjected to the alleged contravention, so could complain about it themselves
      `same respondent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether all their complaints relate to, or arise out of, the conduct of the same person
      `related circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether all their complaints relate to, or arise out of, the same, similar or related circumstances
      `common issue` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether all their complaints give rise to a substantial common issue of law or fact (a judgment for the commissioner; answer as you expect it to be found)
      `day of complaint` IS A DATE @desc The day the representative complaint is made, as an ISO date
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can I make a representative complaint` MEANS
    `s 146(1) -- I may make a representative complaint` `I am a member` `all could complain` `same respondent` `related circumstances` `common issue` `day of complaint`

-- new s 146(2): a registered employee organisation may make one for a class "if" (a) all members of the class are its
-- members; (b) the alleged contravention is a work-related matter; (c) s 146(1)(a) and (b) apply. "a registered
-- employee organisation" is the grant's own subject, not an "if" limb: a body that is not one is outside the grant,
-- NOTHING (2026-11-04 ruling; fork F18).
GIVEN `a registered employee organisation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `all class members are its members` IS A BOOLEAN
      `work-related` IS A BOOLEAN
      `all members could complain` IS A BOOLEAN
      `same respondent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `same or related circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN
      `substantial common issue` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of the complaint` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 146(2) -- my union may make a representative complaint` `a registered employee organisation` `all class members are its members` `work-related` `all members could complain` `same respondent` `same or related circumstances` `substantial common issue` `the day of the complaint` MEANS
    IF `the day` `the day of the complaint` `is before` `1 December 2024`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF NOT (`a registered employee organisation`)
         THEN NOTHING
         ELSE JUST (    `all class members are its members`
                    AND `work-related`
                    AND `all members could complain`
                    AND (`same respondent` AND `same or related circumstances` AND `substantial common issue`))

@export Can my union make a representative complaint for a class of its members that includes me (Anti-Discrimination Act 1991 (Queensland) s 146(2), inserted by the Respect at Work and Other Matters Amendment Act 2024 s 31 from 1 December 2024)? Only an organisation of employees registered under the Industrial Relations Act 2016 or the Fair Work (Registered Organisations) Act 2009, for a work-related contravention, where every class member is a member of it and the s 146(1) tests are met. No answer for a body that is not a registered employee organisation, or for a complaint made before 1 December 2024.
GIVEN `registered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the union is an organisation of employees registered under the Industrial Relations Act 2016 or the Fair Work (Registered Organisations) Act 2009 (Cwlth)
      `all are members` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether every member of the class is a member of the union
      `work-related` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the alleged contravention is a work-related matter
      `all could complain` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether every member of the class was subjected to the alleged contravention, so could complain about it themselves
      `same respondent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether all their complaints relate to, or arise out of, the conduct of the same person
      `related circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether all their complaints relate to, or arise out of, the same, similar or related circumstances
      `common issue` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether all their complaints give rise to a substantial common issue of law or fact (a judgment for the commissioner)
      `day of complaint` IS A DATE @desc The day the representative complaint is made, as an ISO date
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can my union make a representative complaint for us` MEANS
    `s 146(2) -- my union may make a representative complaint` `registered` `all are members` `work-related` `all could complain` `same respondent` `related circumstances` `common issue` `day of complaint`

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `ss 148, 149, 195, 196 -- my own complaint, and opting out`
-- ===================================================================================================================

-- new s 148(1)(b): a class member "is not entitled to make a separate complaint ... unless the person opts out" (a flat
-- negative, JUST FALSE kind). (2), (3): (1)(b) does not apply, for a class member other than the complainant, if the
-- commissioner amends it to a non-representative complaint (s 151), it lapses (ss 142, 167(4)(c), division 5), or,
-- after referral, it lapses under s 193, the tribunal declines to deal with it as representative (s 194) or orders it
-- no longer continue as one (ss 198, 199). s 195(1)(b) repeats the bar before the tribunal, subject to s 148(3).
-- s 149, s 196: a person not in the class, or who opted out, is not prevented.
DECLARE `What has happened to the representative complaint` IS ONE OF
    `nothing of these: it is going ahead as a representative complaint`
    `the commissioner amended it to be a non-representative complaint (s 151)`
    `it lapsed before the commissioner (s 142, s 167(4)(c) or chapter 7 part 1 division 5)`
    `after referral to the tribunal, it lapsed (s 193)`
    `the tribunal decided not to deal with it as a representative complaint (s 194)`
    `the tribunal ordered it no longer continue as a representative complaint (s 198 or s 199)`

DECLARE `Can I make my own complaint` IS ONE OF
    `yes: you are not a member of the class, so the representative complaint does not prevent you (s 149(1), s 196(1))`
    `yes: you opted out, so the representative complaint does not prevent you (s 149(2), s 196(2))`
    `yes: the bar on a separate complaint does not apply to you, because of what has happened to the representative complaint (s 148(2) or (3))`
    `no: as a member of the class you are not entitled to make a separate complaint about the same conduct unless you opt out (s 148(1)(b), s 195(1)(b))`
    `not covered: the former law governs this representative complaint (s 285), including whether you may complain separately`

GIVEN `a member of the class` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I opted out` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I am the complainant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `what happened` IS A `What has happened to the representative complaint`
      `the former law continues` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Can I make my own complaint`
`ss 148, 149 -- my own complaint` `a member of the class` `I opted out` `I am the complainant` `what happened` `the former law continues` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the former law continues`
        THEN `not covered: the former law governs this representative complaint (s 285), including whether you may complain separately`
        IF NOT (`a member of the class`)
        THEN `yes: you are not a member of the class, so the representative complaint does not prevent you (s 149(1), s 196(1))`
        IF `I opted out`
        THEN `yes: you opted out, so the representative complaint does not prevent you (s 149(2), s 196(2))`
        IF (NOT (`I am the complainant`)) AND (NOT (`what happened` EQUALS `nothing of these: it is going ahead as a representative complaint`))
        THEN `yes: the bar on a separate complaint does not apply to you, because of what has happened to the representative complaint (s 148(2) or (3))`
        OTHERWISE `no: as a member of the class you are not entitled to make a separate complaint about the same conduct unless you opt out (s 148(1)(b), s 195(1)(b))`

@export Can I make my own complaint about conduct that a representative complaint already covers (Anti-Discrimination Act 1991 (Queensland) ss 148, 149, 195, 196, as the Respect at Work and Other Matters Amendment Act 2024 inserts them)? A class member cannot, unless they opt out, or the representative complaint is amended to a non-representative one, lapses, or the tribunal stops it going ahead as representative. A person outside the class, or who opted out, can.
GIVEN `class member` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are named or otherwise identified in the representative complaint as a person on whose behalf it is made
      `opted out` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have opted out of it by written notice (to the commissioner, or to the tribunal before its opt-out date)
      `complainant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are the person who made the representative complaint (or were substituted as its complainant)
      `what happened` IS A `What has happened to the representative complaint` @desc What has happened to the representative complaint, if any of the listed events
      `old law continues` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the commissioner accepted the representative complaint before 1 December 2024 and it was still being dealt with on that day (then the former law governs it, s 285)
GIVETH A `Can I make my own complaint`
`Can I make my own complaint` MEANS
    `ss 148, 149 -- my own complaint` `class member` `opted out` `complainant` `what happened` `old law continues`

-- new s 148(1)(a): a class member "may, by written notice given to the commissioner at any time before the complaint is
-- finally dealt with by the commissioner, opt out". new s 195(1)(a), (3): before the tribunal, "before the date fixed"
-- (the opt-out date); s 195(4) a later date may be fixed (asked as the date now fixed). A period the text fixes:
-- outside it, JUST FALSE kind. "Before" the opt-out date: notice on that date is too late (fork F8).
DECLARE `Where the representative complaint is` IS ONE OF
    `with the commissioner`
    `referred to the tribunal`

DECLARE `Can I opt out` IS ONE OF
    `yes: you may opt out by written notice to the commissioner before the commissioner finally deals with the complaint (s 148(1)(a))`
    `no: the commissioner has finally dealt with the complaint`
    `yes: you may opt out by written notice to the tribunal before the opt-out date it fixed (s 195(1)(a))`
    `no: the opt-out date the tribunal fixed has come (s 195(1)(a)); the tribunal may fix a later one on application (s 195(4))`
    `not covered: the former law governs this representative complaint (s 285), including opting out`

GIVEN `where it is` IS A `Where the representative complaint is`
      `finally dealt with by the commissioner` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the opt-out date` IS A DATE
      `the day of my notice` IS A DATE
      `the former law continues` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Can I opt out`
`ss 148(1)(a), 195 -- opting out` `where it is` `finally dealt with by the commissioner` `the opt-out date` `the day of my notice` `the former law continues` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the former law continues`
        THEN `not covered: the former law governs this representative complaint (s 285), including opting out`
        IF `where it is` EQUALS `with the commissioner`
        THEN IF `finally dealt with by the commissioner`
             THEN `no: the commissioner has finally dealt with the complaint`
             ELSE `yes: you may opt out by written notice to the commissioner before the commissioner finally deals with the complaint (s 148(1)(a))`
        IF `the day` `the day of my notice` `is before` `the opt-out date`
        THEN `yes: you may opt out by written notice to the tribunal before the opt-out date it fixed (s 195(1)(a))`
        OTHERWISE `no: the opt-out date the tribunal fixed has come (s 195(1)(a)); the tribunal may fix a later one on application (s 195(4))`

@export Can I still opt out of a representative complaint that includes me (Anti-Discrimination Act 1991 (Queensland) ss 148(1)(a) and 195, as the Respect at Work and Other Matters Amendment Act 2024 inserts them)? With the commissioner: by written notice any time before the commissioner finally deals with it. In the tribunal: by written notice before the opt-out date the tribunal fixes.
GIVEN `where it is` IS A `Where the representative complaint is` @desc Whether the representative complaint is with the commissioner, or has been referred to the tribunal
      `finally dealt with` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it is with the commissioner, whether the commissioner has finally dealt with it
      `opt-out date` IS A DATE @desc If it is in the tribunal, the opt-out date the tribunal has fixed (or the later date it has since fixed), as an ISO date; otherwise any date
      `day of notice` IS A DATE @desc The day you give, or would give, your written notice of opting out, as an ISO date
      `old law continues` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the commissioner accepted the representative complaint before 1 December 2024 and it was still being dealt with on that day (then the former law governs it, s 285)
GIVETH A `Can I opt out`
`Can I opt out of the representative complaint` MEANS
    `ss 148(1)(a), 195 -- opting out` `where it is` `finally dealt with` `opt-out date` `day of notice` `old law continues`

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `s 209(5) -- costs`
-- ===================================================================================================================

-- new s 209(5) (s 48(10), (12)): "The tribunal may order costs in a complaint as follows-- (a) for a representative
-- complaint--against the complainant or the respondent, but not against a class member for the complaint other than
-- the complainant; (b) otherwise--as provided under the relevant tribunal Act." The relevant tribunal Act (the QCAT Act
-- or the Industrial Relations Act 2016) is not deposited here: "not covered".
DECLARE `My role in the complaint` IS ONE OF
    `the complainant`
    `a class member, not the complainant`
    `the respondent`

DECLARE `Can costs be ordered against me` IS ONE OF
    `yes: in a representative complaint the tribunal may order costs against the complainant or the respondent (s 209(5)(a))`
    `no: in a representative complaint costs may not be ordered against a class member other than the complainant (s 209(5)(a))`
    `not covered: outside a representative complaint, costs are as the relevant tribunal Act provides (s 209(5)(b)), which is not encoded here`
    `not covered: the former law governs this representative complaint (s 285), including costs`

GIVEN `representative` IS A BOOLEAN
      `my role` IS A `My role in the complaint`
      `the former law continues` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Can costs be ordered against me`
`s 209(5) -- costs` `representative` `my role` `the former law continues` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`representative`)
        THEN `not covered: outside a representative complaint, costs are as the relevant tribunal Act provides (s 209(5)(b)), which is not encoded here`
        IF `the former law continues`
        THEN `not covered: the former law governs this representative complaint (s 285), including costs`
        IF `my role` EQUALS `a class member, not the complainant`
        THEN `no: in a representative complaint costs may not be ordered against a class member other than the complainant (s 209(5)(a))`
        OTHERWISE `yes: in a representative complaint the tribunal may order costs against the complainant or the respondent (s 209(5)(a))`

@export Can the tribunal order me to pay costs in an anti-discrimination complaint (Anti-Discrimination Act 1991 (Queensland) s 209(5), as the Respect at Work and Other Matters Amendment Act 2024 s 48 inserts it from 1 December 2024)? In a representative complaint costs may be ordered against the complainant or the respondent, but never against a class member who is not the complainant. Otherwise the tribunal's own Act decides.
GIVEN `representative` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the complaint is a representative complaint (made on behalf of a class of people)
      `role` IS A `My role in the complaint` @desc Your role: the complainant; a class member who is not the complainant; or the respondent
      `old law continues` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the commissioner accepted the representative complaint before 1 December 2024 and it was still being dealt with on that day (then the former law governs it, s 285)
GIVETH A `Can costs be ordered against me`
`Can costs be ordered against me` MEANS
    `s 209(5) -- costs` `representative` `role` `old law continues`

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `ss 204, 205, 285A -- who must prove what`
-- ===================================================================================================================

-- new s 204 (s 47A): in a complaint proceeding, if there are facts from which it could be decided, absent any other
-- explanation, that the respondent contravened the provision, the respondent is taken to have contravened it, unless
-- the respondent proves on the balance of probabilities that it did not. new s 205: a person relying on an exemption
-- must prove it applies. new s 285A (as passed): new ss 204 and 205 do not apply to (a) a complaint made before "the
-- commencement" and not finally dealt with immediately before it, or (b) a complaint made after it about a
-- contravention before it; former ss 204 to 206 (not deposited) continue.
--
-- s 47A commenced on 1 December 2024 (fork F1), but s 285A is in the 1 July 2025 group. The Anti-Discrimination Act
-- 1991 in force on 6 November 2026 has instead s 285AA (inserted by later legislation): the same two cases, measured
-- from "the commencement of section 7B of the amendment Act", and "taken to have applied from 1 December 2024". The
-- exported question follows s 285AA, the law as it now stands in the deposited 1991 Act; the as-passed reading is kept
-- beside it for finding 3.
DECLARE `Who must prove what` IS ONE OF
    `new s 204: if there are facts from which it could be decided, in the absence of any other explanation, that the respondent contravened the Act, the respondent is taken to have done so unless it proves on the balance of probabilities that it did not; a respondent relying on an exemption must prove it applies (s 205)`
    `former ss 204 to 206 continue to apply to your complaint (s 285AA of the Anti-Discrimination Act 1991; s 285A of the amending Act as passed); their text is not deposited here`

GIVEN `the day of the contravention` IS A DATE
      `the day of the complaint` IS A DATE
      `the July 2025 changes have commenced` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day they commenced` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Who must prove what`
`ss 204, 205, 285AA -- the burden of proof now` `the day of the contravention` `the day of the complaint` `the July 2025 changes have commenced` `the day they commenced` MEANS
    IF      `the July 2025 changes are in force on` `the July 2025 changes have commenced` `the day they commenced` `the day of the complaint`
        AND `the July 2025 changes are in force on` `the July 2025 changes have commenced` `the day they commenced` `the day of the contravention`
    THEN `new s 204: if there are facts from which it could be decided, in the absence of any other explanation, that the respondent contravened the Act, the respondent is taken to have done so unless it proves on the balance of probabilities that it did not; a respondent relying on an exemption must prove it applies (s 205)`
    ELSE `former ss 204 to 206 continue to apply to your complaint (s 285AA of the Anti-Discrimination Act 1991; s 285A of the amending Act as passed); their text is not deposited here`

-- The amending Act alone, as passed: new ss 204 and 205 from 1 December 2024 (s 47A, s 2(1)(b)); s 285A only once the
-- 1 July 2025 group commences. Asked of a tribunal deciding the complaint on a given day. Not exported (finding 3).
GIVEN `the day of the contravention` IS A DATE
      `the day of the complaint` IS A DATE
      `the day of the decision` IS A DATE
      `the July 2025 changes have commenced` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day they commenced` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `ss 204, 205, 285A -- new burden of proof under the Act as passed` `the day of the contravention` `the day of the complaint` `the day of the decision` `the July 2025 changes have commenced` `the day they commenced` IF
    IF `the day` `the day of the decision` `is before` `1 December 2024`
    THEN FALSE
    ELSE IF NOT (`the July 2025 changes are in force on` `the July 2025 changes have commenced` `the day they commenced` `the day of the decision`)
         THEN TRUE
         ELSE     `the July 2025 changes are in force on` `the July 2025 changes have commenced` `the day they commenced` `the day of the complaint`
              AND `the July 2025 changes are in force on` `the July 2025 changes have commenced` `the day they commenced` `the day of the contravention`

@export Who has to prove what in my anti-discrimination complaint before the tribunal (Anti-Discrimination Act 1991 (Queensland) ss 204, 205, as the Respect at Work and Other Matters Amendment Act 2024 s 47A replaced them)? Under the new rule the respondent is taken to have contravened the Act if the facts point that way, unless it proves otherwise. It reaches only complaints made, about conduct that happened, on or after the commencement of the amending Act's 1 July 2025 group (s 285AA); otherwise the former rules apply.
GIVEN `day of contravention` IS A DATE @desc The day the alleged contravention happened, as an ISO date
      `day of complaint` IS A DATE @desc The day the complaint was made to the commissioner, as an ISO date
      `July 2025 changes commenced` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the changes the amending Act set for 1 July 2025 (in particular its s 7B) have commenced; they were not in the Anti-Discrimination Act 1991 in force on 6 November 2026, so check the Queensland legislation register
      `July 2025 changes day` IS A DATE @desc If they have commenced, the day they did, as an ISO date; otherwise any date
GIVETH A `Who must prove what`
`Who must prove what in my complaint` MEANS
    `ss 204, 205, 285AA -- the burden of proof now` `day of contravention` `day of complaint` `July 2025 changes commenced` `July 2025 changes day`
